 ["A",3,"A guesthouse in Maafushi reviews expected sales, costs and profits for a new island-hopping tour before it spends money on boats. Which stage of new product development is this?",["Business analysis","Concept testing","Idea screening","Product development"],"Business analysis checks sales, costs and profit forecasts against company goals."],
 ["A",3,"Sales of an airline snack box are falling, but it still makes a small profit. The airline cuts its marketing spending and keeps selling the box for now. Which strategy is this?",["Harvesting the product","Modifying the market","Penetration pricing","Concept testing"],"Harvesting means cutting costs on a declining product while it still makes money."]
